## Scope
Problem 30006081, queue row 1855 remains **unsolved**, Turns **5/5**. This draft records five scoped partial results, not a solution of the umbrella problem and not a novelty claim:
- sharp expected minimax cost pn, not a pointwise lower bound;
- known row-space priors and squared-additive tails;
- r-query EP reconstruction;
- known-range rank-one candidate geometry;
- constant-real-drift Dirichlet PDE bounds only.

The real finite-query theorem is credited to Theorem 5.1 of the arXiv preprint *Transpose-free linear algebra*. Complex-field, aspect-ratio, expected-cost and norm extensions have separate proofs. General asymmetric geometry and general PDE questions remain unresolved.

## Verification
The frozen sixteen-file authored package passed independent full normal and optimized replay, full transformed-AST comparison, complete numerical-output comparison, and 48 adversarial mutation controls. Root package manifest SHA-256: `16ce4646d324afc8037721cf4c23d15010ea159068e86d30058cfb2861a10a2d`.

The only other file is the existing full QUEUE, with only row 1855 Status, Turns and Findings changed; unrelated bytes and existing links are preserved. No copied source documents, datasets or private coordination files are included. Post-publication pinned readback verification will be recorded separately. No merge or main mutation is requested.
